Nice to hear from you and thanks for your interest. We have not implemented that functionality, because we do not have datasets that use those connector types.

The first question would be how CATMAID returns different connectors. This is what defines the external facing API:

https://github.com/catmaid/CATMAID/blob/ce1dee4485e76c3b33bc751d5440ce8477fb1f43/django/applications/catmaid/urls.py#L216

And this is the function

https://github.com/catmaid/CATMAID/blob/ce1dee4485e76c3b33bc751d5440ce8477fb1f43/django/applications/catmaid/control/connector.py#L524-L560

I actually don't see any reference to connector types - just pre vs post.

@Tom, perhaps you could advise what API endpoint would expose that information? Would one need to look up the kind of connector separately?

All the best,

Greg.

